url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/jack-zarrop-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","title":"Jack Zarrop: Prevention of future deaths report","date":"2023-10-02","coroner":"Anton van Dellen","area":"West London","ref":"2023-0362","categories":["Suicide (from 2015)"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/2023-0362-Response-from-National-Police-Chiefs-Council.pdf","filename":"2023-0362-Response-from-National-Police-Chiefs-Council.pdf","promises":[]},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/2023-0362-Response-from-NHSE.pdf","filename":"2023-0362-Response-from-NHSE.pdf","promises":[{"id":667,"quote":"NHS England is the responsible organisation for the commissioning of healthcare into prisons, which is devolved to regional teams. Commissioning healthcare in prisons is done on a principle of equivalence, which has been defined by the Royal College of General Practitioners (RCGP) and has been adopted by the National Prison Partnership Board1. The definition broadly states the aim is to ensure people detained in prisons in England, are offered provision of and access to appropriate services and","summary":"Commissioning healthcare in prisons follows equivalence principle defined by RCGP and National Prison Partnership Board","timescale":null}]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/john-condron-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","title":"John Condron: Prevention of future deaths report","date":"2023-10-06","coroner":"Charlotte Keighley","area":"Cheshire","ref":"2023-0374","categories":["Suicide (from 2015)"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/2023-0374-Response-from-Cheshire-Constabulary.pdf","filename":"2023-0374-Response-from-Cheshire-Constabulary.pdf","promises":[{"id":366,"quote":"The Constabulary has now reviewed the existing Suspect Policy and Procedure, that was originally introduced in August 2023 (i